PATCH 343 -- FUN_0000_6980 (NovaLogic Voxel-Space column raycaster): model the SMC-patched PER-RAY
STEP + fix the rotation-multiply SIGNEDNESS.  Two interlocking defect classes patch 342 did NOT
cover; together they were the ROOT CAUSE of the mission-terrain "solid-column / few-dark-colours"
residual.  Mission-path only (6980 is never reached by the 25 menu/intro/settings verify flows);
default boot unaffected.

DEFECT A -- SMC PER-RAY STEP (asm-verified vs re_out/fist_image.bin @ ext 0x6980..0x6bf6, LE:32 PM):
  ; the inner span-loop's coordinate step is SELF-MODIFYING: written per depth into the add/sub imms
  6a9d: imul ds:0x9100     ; edx = (4224[d] * 9100) >> 32   (signed)
  6aa3: mov ds:0x6ad2,edx  ; -> IMM32 operand of `add ebx,IMM32` @ 6ad0   (fwd X step)
  6aa9: mov ds:0x6b52,edx  ; -> IMM32 operand of `sub ebx,IMM32` @ 6b50   (rev X step, copy)
  6ab1: imul ds:0x90fc     ; edx = (4224[d] * 90fc) >> 32   (signed)
  6ab7: mov ds:0x6ad8,edx  ; -> IMM32 operand of `sub ebp,IMM32` @ 6ad6   (fwd Y step)
  6abd: mov ds:0x6b58,edx  ; -> IMM32 operand of `add ebp,IMM32` @ 6b56   (rev Y step, copy)
  6ad0: add ebx,0x7fffffff ; ebx += [6ad2]      6ad6: sub ebp,0x7fffffff ; ebp -= [6ad8]
  6b50: sub ebx,0x7fffffff ; ebx -= [6b52]      6b56: add ebp,0x7fffffff ; ebp += [6b58]
Ghidra could not model the SMC -> it stepped the ray by the UN-PATCHED static immediates
(`uVar6 + 0x7fffffff` / `uVar11 + 0x80000001`, a ~2^31 garbage step), so EVERY screen column swept
the identical (depth-center) coordinate -> the tile was written with byte-identical content in every
column (the "solid column").  ALSO the SMC operand stores uRam00006ad2/6ad8/6b52/6b58 are typed
undefined2 (16-bit) while the operands are 32-bit IMM32 -> a 16-bit store truncates the signed step;
widened to full 32-bit here.

DEFECT B -- ROTATION-MULTIPLY SIGNEDNESS: the world-rotation basis DAT_0000_90fc/9100 is typed
undefined4 (== uint32_t), so `(longlong)DAT_0000_9100` ZERO-extends (0x9e669af4 -> +2.65e9) while
the asm `imul ds:0x9100` is SIGNED (0x9e669af4 -> -1.64e9).  The step/center then used the wrong sign
(e.g. fwd X step +4036 unsigned vs -2488 signed) -> the ray marched a too-narrow coordinate range
(port tile max colour 151, distinct 22 vs the asm-faithful 228 / ~59).  Cast the rotation operands to
signed `(int)` at the center (6a72..6a91) and step (6a9d/6ab1) multiplies to match the signed imul.
(Ghidra "signed imul/sar semantics" artifact class.)

THE FIX (faithful, control-flow 1:1): store the full 32-bit SIGNED step into the SMC operand slots
(0x6ad2/0x6ad8 fwd, 0x6b52/0x6b58 rev = the asm copies), consume them in the inner-loop sweep with
the asm's exact signs, and sign-extend the rotation operands.  Proven standalone: FIST_6980PROVE
(tools/native_main.c) -> the port's real 6980 tile goes from 5 distinct solid columns to a depth-
varied terrain matching a from-scratch asm-faithful Python march of 6980 byte-for-byte.

NB the sibling voxel functions (other switch-case decompiles at ext ~0x6d80..) carry the identical
static-step + unsigned-rotation classes + are un-rebased; they are NOT reached (op-0x24 wiring not
landed) and left as documented latent debt -- fix them when their path lands.

